  "body": "### What happened\n\nI'm working on Setup2.   I changed the WCS from Setup1.   The machine orientation did not change as it should.  The part shows stock top and clearance using the WCS from Setup1.\n\n<img width=\"1311\" height=\"836\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e96335cb-7bc5-400d-9143-58deaaa7dc37\" />\n\nWhen I select a top face to machine, I get this error message:\ngeometry selection not updated: invalid parameters: face 0xdc461ed05cf94951 of 'End Caps-End capSupport Plate' is not horizontal - a facing pass needs a floor; machine its boundary with a 2D Contour instead\n\nI don't want to do a 2D Contour using the WCS of Setup1.  I want to do a facing operation using the new part orientation.   \n\nIf I Generate, it faces the wrong face, using the wrong orientation.  Notice the facing operation does not match the WCS orientation.\n\n<img width=\"1311\" height=\"836\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed02f780-8b47-426b-b762-3748e1398f2e\" />\n\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSetup Setup1\nCreate Setup2\nChange Setup2's WCS different from Setup 1.\nSelect a 2D facing operation.\nSelect a suitable face.\n\n\n### camcraft version and OS\n\nCamCraft 0.19.0 (release build) Build time: 2026-11-13 16:01 UTC Source commit: a2b357b48c6af61952c92a379ec426757d8a5cd8-dirty Platform: linux x86_64 GPU: gpu: adapter \"NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070\" via vulkan Project: /home/me/Documents/Version 19 test.camproj Units: Millimeters Machine: Camcraft Tormach 1100MX (Mill, from built-in: Tormach 1100MX) Document: 2 setup(s), 1 model(s), 5 tool(s), 2 operation(s) (2 ok, 0 stale, 0 never generated) Status: generated Face2: 120 moves (1 plunge(s) @ 300, 1 level(s), 0 arc(s)), 0 warning(s)\n\n### Screenshots or recording\n\n_No response_",
